    "subtitle": "How Korea trades and shares culture with China, Japan, and Russia.",
    "body": "Korea has three close neighbors. China, Japan, and Russia all sit near us on the map.\n\nBecause they are close, we share much with them. China is a huge land to our west. Many Korean factories sell phones and cars there.\n\nJapan lies across the sea to our east. Korean singers and shows are loved in Japan, and we enjoy their cartoons too.\n\nRussia stretches far to our north. It sends us gas and wood, and we send it ships.\n\nWe also trade food, music, and ideas every day. Sharing like this is called <mark>cultural exchange</mark>.\n\nWhen we learn about our neighbors, we understand them better. Good neighbors talk, trade, and grow together.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/venus/2026-07/12.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Korea at the center, sharing goods and culture with China, Japan, and Russia all around it."
